The tx was left unmined in the mempool (chain tip unchanged at 113).

--- 4. Why an Orchard note cannot be funded on this chain (ZIP 258) ---
ZIP 258, "Consensus rules from NU6.3 activation" (https://zips.z.cash/zip-0258):
  * "A coinbase transaction MUST NOT contain any Orchard-pool Actions; that is, its Orchard
     component MUST be empty."
  * "No new value may enter the Orchard pool: for every transaction,
     vOrchardPoolBalance >= 0 (so the encoded valueBalanceOrchard is nonnegative).
     Value may still leave the Orchard pool, including across the turnstile into the
     Ironwood pool."
The Ironwood Book, "Value Movement After NU6.3":
  "After NU6.3 activation, no funds can flow into the Orchard pool. Transactions can still
   spend Orchard-pool funds, and zero-balance Orchard-pool actions are still allowed, but the
   Orchard pool's value balance must not be negative."

Funding an Orchard-pool note with any positive value requires valueBalanceOrchard < 0, which
Zebra rejects after NU6.3. Therefore, on a regtest where NU6.3 activates at height 2, the
Orchard tree can never receive a commitment and no Orchard-pool note can ever exist.

--- 5. Consequence for P4 ---
The P4 follow-up asked for an Orchard-pool note spent into Ironwood with a real witness and a
real Orchard anchor. There is no such note and no such anchor on this chain:
  * The only Orchard anchor Zebra knows is the empty-tree root ae2935f1...5d82f.
  * The P4 test's broadcast rejection remains the exact error:
    {"code":-25,"message":"failed to validate tx: WtxId(\"private\"), error: transaction did not
     pass consensus validation: could not contextually validate transaction on best chain:
     unknown Orchard anchor: Root(\"d9ed557565d281bc804b72339bbfcdd41d95167adc5bfd088d0f5da6440fb008\"),
     None, index in block: None, transaction::Hash(...)"}

The only way to exercise a real Orchard-pool note is a regtest whose NU6.3 activation height is
ABOVE the funding height (so blocks mined before activation can pay an Orchard receiver and be
spent after activation). That requires changing config/regtest/zebra.toml's activation schedule
and wiping/re-initialising the chain, which would invalidate the funded state behind the P2/P3
evidence. Not done here; reported as a limitation.
